<!--
  Body starts here. Plain HTML — <p>, <ul>, <h2>, <table>, <blockquote>, <code>.
  Do not add an <h1>; the page supplies one from the title above.

  Two rules that matter for whether this entry gets found and cited:

  1. THE ISLAND TEST. Every <h2> section must make sense if it is the only
     thing a reader ever sees. Retrieval engines return passages, not pages.
     A paragraph beginning "This approach also..." is unquotable.

  2. KEEP THE NUMBERS. "Cut RMSE from 0.081 to 0.049 across 412 surface fits"
     is citable. "Improved accuracy substantially" is not.

  Rename this file to YYYY-MM-DD-a-short-slug.html — the filename becomes the
  URL — then run: python3 scripts/build_site.py
-->

<h2>What I expected</h2>
<p>
